      "passed": false,
      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports that the alpha wave envelope was subjected to secondary differentiation to produce positive (Ap) and negative (An) acceleration values, but it does not support the specific interpretation that negative acceleration “reflects moments when the envelope’s change is bending downward during the waxing and waning of alpha activity.”",
        "The claim that negative acceleration was “used in the study as part of the comparison with positive acceleration” is broadly supported (the study computed Ap and An and used their ratio Ap-An), but the definition includes the unsupported “bending downward” explanation."
